Q: How can I prevent Windows PowerShell from breaking my bun/npm commands A: <p>If you reference <code>npm.cmd</code> directly instead of <code>npm</code> and handle the space correctly, the error does not occur. It seems that the error is caused by Bun incorrectly when there is a space in the path.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, this only works on Windows in this case.</p>
<p><strong>package.json</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;scripts&quot;: {
    &quot;bump&quot;: &quot;git add . &amp;&amp; 'C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\npm.cmd' version patch -m 'Release %s' &amp;&amp; git push origin master --tags&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/11328" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>oven-sh/bun</code> issue #11328 - Error calling cmd/bat scripts when both args and path contain spaces</a></li>
</ul>
<p>If you want to run it on multiple systems, even before the bug is fixed, then creating a script might be the best approach:</p>
<p><strong>./scripts/bump.js</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import { execSync } from &quot;child_process&quot;;

execSync(&quot;git add .&quot;, { stdio: &quot;inherit&quot; });
execSync(&quot;npm version patch -m \&quot;Release %s\&quot;&quot;, { stdio: &quot;inherit&quot; });
execSync(&quot;git push origin master --tags&quot;, { stdio: &quot;inherit&quot; });
</code></pre>
<p><strong>package.json</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;scripts&quot;: {
    &quot;bump&quot;: &quot;node scripts/bump.js&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
